{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"2395a74d-cb65-4046-9716-734c8486fa51","step_index":107,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"The root causes of the Intervals.icu connection failures have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/ANSWER.md) and the integration has been fixed.\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized Error**:\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was a top-level document navigation link (`\u003ca class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`). The SPA stored auth tokens in `localStorage` and sent them via `Authorization: Bearer` on `fetch` calls, so regular browser navigation did not send the header, resulting in HTTP 401.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/static/app.js) to pass the token as a query parameter (`?token=...`) and updated `current_user` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L148-L157) to accept tokens from both the query string and the `Authorization` header.\n\n2. **Missing `response_type=code` in Authorize Request**:\n   - **Cause**: `auth_init` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L201-L208) omitted `response_type=code` when constructing the redirect URL to `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize`. Standard OAuth 2.0 (RFC 6749) and Intervals.icu require `response_type=code`, resulting in HTTP 400 `{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}`.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\"response_type\": \"code\"` to the authorization query parameters in `auth_init`.\n\n3. **Premature Disconnection (\"expired, reconnect\") After 1 Hour**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu issues long-lived OAuth tokens without `expires_in` or `refresh_token`. `store_connection` in `server.py` defaulted missing `expires_in` values to 3600 seconds (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the background `refresh_tokens()` worker marked connections as `\"expired, reconnect\"` when they neared 1 hour without a refresh token.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L64-L108) so that tokens lacking `expires_in` are stored with `expires_at = None`, and configured `refresh_tokens()` to ignore connections that do not specify an expiry time.\n","duration_seconds":8.618591,"usage":{"input_tokens":2291,"output_tokens":601,"thinking_tokens":25,"cache_read_tokens":76133,"total_tokens":2892}}}
{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2395a74d-cb65-4046-9716-734c8486fa51","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root causes of the Intervals.icu connection failures have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/ANSWER.md) and the integration has been fixed.\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button 401 Unauthorized Error**:\n   - **Cause**: The \"Connect Intervals.icu\" button was a top-level document navigation link (`\u003ca class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`). The SPA stored auth tokens in `localStorage` and sent them via `Authorization: Bearer` on `fetch` calls, so regular browser navigation did not send the header, resulting in HTTP 401.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/static/app.js) to pass the token as a query parameter (`?token=...`) and updated `current_user` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L148-L157) to accept tokens from both the query string and the `Authorization` header.\n\n2. **Missing `response_type=code` in Authorize Request**:\n   - **Cause**: `auth_init` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L201-L208) omitted `response_type=code` when constructing the redirect URL to `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize`. Standard OAuth 2.0 (RFC 6749) and Intervals.icu require `response_type=code`, resulting in HTTP 400 `{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}`.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\"response_type\": \"code\"` to the authorization query parameters in `auth_init`.\n\n3. **Premature Disconnection (\"expired, reconnect\") After 1 Hour**:\n   - **Cause**: Intervals.icu issues long-lived OAuth tokens without `expires_in` or `refresh_token`. `store_connection` in `server.py` defaulted missing `expires_in` values to 3600 seconds (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the background `refresh_tokens()` worker marked connections as `\"expired, reconnect\"` when they neared 1 hour without a refresh token.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-EtQiB7/server.py#L64-L108) so that tokens lacking `expires_in` are stored with `expires_at = None`, and configured `refresh_tokens()` to ignore connections that do not specify an expiry time.\n","duration_seconds":429.61133,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":252435,"output_tokens":38272,"thinking_tokens":30381,"cache_read_tokens":2320616,"total_tokens":290707}}}
